<gpx version="1.1" creator="book_route.py" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
<metadata><name>Meadows Creek Trail loop (with the East Fork and Teacup Lake trails)</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:202-5: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="45.320470" lon="-121.619952"><ele>1308.3</ele><name>Teacup Lake Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:teacup-lake-sno-park (OSM parking way/144835813); confidence: high; pdf_page: 204; quote: This 3.3-mile Intermediate trail starts at Teacup Lake Sno-Park and at first parallels Highway 35 northeast</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.302220" lon="-121.603446"><ele>1288.4</ele><name>Upper Junction of Pocket Creek</name><desc>source: OSM junction of Forest Road 3540 and 3540-640, as in or-vielbig-2e_204-1; the OSM Meadows Creek Trail piste (way 475564020) ends 60 m east; confidence: high; pdf_page: 205; book_elev_ft: 4200; quote: It finally reaches a huge clearcut that climbs moderately to the Upper Junction of Pocket Creek, directly under Bennett Ridge.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.309802" lon="-121.628009"><ele>1315.5</ele><name>East Fork Trail west end (Teacup Lake Trail / Pocket Creek Tie Trail clearcut)</name><desc>source: OSM node 33434179 on Forest Road 3540, 37 m from the south end of the Teacup Lake Trail piste (way 475562024) and 24 m from the end of the Pocket Creek - Bennett Pass Tie trail 682; confidence: high; pdf_page: 207; quote: At its west end the trail ends at a clearcut where two other trails join--Pocket Creek Tie Trail ... and the 1.5-mile Teacup Lake Trail coming from Teacup Lake Sno-Park.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.320470" lon="-121.619952"><ele>1308.3</ele><name>Teacup Lake Sno-Park (finish)</name><desc>source: as start; confidence: high; pdf_page: 205; quote: From the south end of Teacup Lake Sno-Park, ski the trail 300 yards to a road and follow it 120 yards.</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>Meadows Creek Trail loop (with the East Fork and Teacup Lake trails)</name><desc>1. Teacup Lake Sno-Park -&gt; Upper Junction of Pocket Creek: osm (high), 3.08 mi | 2. Upper Junction of Pocket Creek -&gt; East Fork Trail west end (Teacup Lake Trail / Pocket Creek Tie Trail clearcut): osm (high), 1.61 mi | 3. East Fork Trail west end (Teacup Lake Trail / Pocket Creek Tie Trail clearcut) -&gt; Teacup Lake Sno-Park (finish): osm (medium), 1.46 mi</desc>
